# ── Added 2026-08-07 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything below was untracked AND unignored: 962 files, 74 GB. Nothing here
# was lost by ignoring it — the files stay on disk, they just stop being one
# `git add -A` away from a push that GitHub would reject anyway.

# Model weights and quantised artifacts — 73 GB of the 74. GitHub hard-rejects
# files over 100 MB and nine of these are 100 MB to 16 GB. These live on the
# huggingface remote, not here. Zero were tracked when this rule was added.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.pt
models/base/
models/adapters/
models/minilm-ov/
ollama/*.gguf
codette-gguf/
codette-lora/
behavioral-lora-f16-gguf/
behavioral_safetensors/
adapters/hf_download/
adapters/hf_download_v4/

# Python bytecode — 243 files under reasoning_forge alone
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Runtime logs — the rule lives at the top of this file, not here.
#
# 2026-08-11: this section repeated `logs/` as a blanket directory rule. The
# last matching pattern wins, so it silently reinstated exactly what the
# 2026-08-03 change was made to remove — `git check-ignore -v
# logs/some_new_module.py` named THIS line, not `logs/*.log`. Five Python
# modules that exist nowhere else in the repository were invisible for that
# reason once already.
#
# The blanket rule is removed and not repeated. Actual .log files remain
# ignored by `logs/*.log` and `*.log` above, which covers runtime output
# including logs/governor_decisions.log — kept on disk so a restart cannot
# erase the governor's own record, kept out of git because it is a
# minute-by-minute trace of when Jonathan is talking to her.
*.log

# Local pre-edit backups. Kept on disk deliberately (nothing is erased here),
# but they are point-in-time copies of files that are already in history.
_sync_backup/
_backup_prompt_wiring_*/

# Nested clone: codette-demo-space is its own git repository with its own
# remote (418 MB). Committing it would create a broken gitlink.
codette-demo-space/

# Editor state
.vscode/

# Adapter tokenizer / checkpoint artifacts — model files, 17 MB each
adapters/**/tokenizer.json
adapters/**/checkpoint-*/

# Personal identity material — encrypted, but personal and this repo is public
data/identities/

# Runtime learned state and shadow telemetry (changes every session)
data/optimizer_state.json
data/optimizer_shadow.jsonl

# Nexis engine live memory + cocoon scratch (written continuously)
reasoning_forge/.logs/

# OpenVINO compiled-blob cache — roughly model-sized, and a build artifact of
# (model, device, driver) rather than source. OpenVINO invalidates it itself
# when any of those change, so it is safe to delete and must not be committed.
# Set CODETTE_OV_CACHE_DIR to relocate it outside the tree entirely.
openvino_backend/.ov_cache/
